# xLaDe Roadmap

This document explains the core objectives of xLaDe.
This is not an engineering roadmap. For that, please read versioned roadmaps according to xLaDe version.
This is more like an overall direction of our project.

---

## Initial Plan

When we started this project, these were our original goals, stated in exact same order.
These are only stated for historical reference.

1. Humanized proof
2. Tactics improvement
3. Understanding error and correction
4. Creating an IDE
5. Adding visual input in Lean
6. Using machine learning and AI
7. Adding inbuilt community for communication and help
8. Lean running in mobiles and all the possible devices
9. Integration with other proof assistants
10. Lean4 language improvement

---

## Objectives

After starting and working on this project, our overall direction has been changed due to practicality and intentions.
We write our current long-term goals as follows:

1. Reproducible environments for Lean 4 projects
2. Ecosystem level tools and help for workflow enhancement
3. Integration with external tools, agents, ecosystem, etc.

The objectives are intentionally few and broad. 
xLaDe is intentionally a simple and boring tool.

